{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-su2-basis","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:su2-basis","kind":"definition","title":"$\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ basis","tags":["lie-algebra","su2"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.PathIntegrals.SU2Basis","text":"su2-basis.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:su2-basis\"></a><p>Write <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau_1,\\tau_2,\\tau_3</code> for the Pauli matrices and define the basis:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">e_a=-\\tfrac{i}{2}\\tau_a,\\qquad a=1,2,3.</code></pre>\n<p>The Lie bracket is:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">[e_a,e_b]=\\epsilon_{abc}e_c.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.md","heading":"Definition","number":"6.5.1"}
